Description: Add MC XCOFF base-class sources to swiftshader's bundled LLVM PPC target.
 PPCXCOFFObjectWriter.cpp and PPCMCAsmInfo.cpp subclass
 MCXCOFFObjectTargetWriter and MCAsmInfoXCOFF respectively, but the
 corresponding .cpp files defining those base classes are not compiled into
 swiftshader's LLVM MC library. This produces undefined-symbol link errors
 in libvk_swiftshader.so on ppc64le. Linux ppc64le uses ELF, not XCOFF, so
 the XCOFF backend is effectively dead code — but the vtables and destructors
 still need to link.
 .
 Add the two base-class sources to the swiftshader_llvm_ppc source set so
 they only compile when PPC is targeted.

--- a/third_party/swiftshader/third_party/llvm-10.0/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/swiftshader/third_party/llvm-10.0/BUILD.gn
@@ -1216,6 +1216,8 @@ swiftshader_llvm_source_set("swiftshader_llvm_mips") {
 
 swiftshader_llvm_source_set("swiftshader_llvm_ppc") {
   sources = [
+    "llvm/lib/MC/MCAsmInfoXCOFF.cpp",
+    "llvm/lib/MC/MCXCOFFObjectTargetWriter.cpp",
     "llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/AsmParser/PPCAsmParser.cpp",
     "llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/Disassembler/PPCDisassembler.cpp",
     "llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/MCTargetDesc/PPCAsmBackend.cpp",
